<title>SOUTH KOREA: BOK steps in to ease won's fall vs dollar - dealers.</title>
<headline>BOK steps in to ease won's fall vs dollar - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central bank of Korea intervened in the interbank market in early afternoon on Tuesday to slow the won's decline versus the dollar, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The central bank never comments on intervention.</p>
<p>Dealers said the central bank stepped in when the won fell to an intraday low of 829.80. The won soon bounced back up to 828.50.</p>
<p>&quot;The central bank came in to prevent the dollar from rising to 830,&quot; said a local dealer. &quot;The market is still short in dollars, so banks are buying.&quot;</p>
<p>The bank sold about $500-550 million on Monday.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
</text>
